{"availability":"available","full":"rovelstars/rasmalai","name":"rasmalai","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T04:32:38Z","updated":"2026-10-08T11:08:43Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"rasmalai.rovelstars.com","topics":["language","programming","programming-language","system","systems-programming"],"demo":"https://rasmalai.rovelstars.com/playground","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:27.568Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:27.568Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:27.568Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.385Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:31.180Z","stars":4,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:27.568Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Documentation · Issues · Website · View packages","Rasmalai is a high-performance compiled programming language. It pairs TypeScript-like developer ergonomics with native C-ABI interop, a multi-pass LIR optimizer, a Cranelift JIT for fast dev cycles, and an LLVM AOT backend for release builds. One toolchain covers scripting, native binaries, and a browser playground.","Mainstream systems languages force a choice: ergonomics or control. Rasmalai refuses it — memory safety through ARC with explicit cyclic edges instead of a garbage collector, Python-grade readability with native execution speed, and a standard library that treats files, sockets, threads, and SIMD as first-class citizens rather than FFI afterthoughts."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rovelstars/rasmalai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e79f51196d0fb5e8da2803ca661868ac562f267f70624cf17c002c0d088191e2","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:56:56.109Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:46.972Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Documentation · Issues · Website · View packages","sourceUrl":"https://gith